%erg 0.1
Title: Add 'erg list' command to show all open tickets
Created: 2026-05-20
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-05-20T09:05Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context

`erg ready` shows only unblocked tickets. There is no command to list ALL open tickets
(with or without blockers), their titles, and basic metadata (created date, tags, blocked-by).

The `ready` command is useful for agents picking work, but humans and raid scripts need
to see the full picture: blocked tickets, tagged tickets, everything that's still open.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `erg list [DIR]` prints all open tickets (one line each): ID, title, tags, blocked-by
- [ ] `erg list --json [DIR]` outputs JSON array for script consumption
- [ ] `erg list --all [DIR]` includes closed tickets (default: open only)
- [ ] Tickets sorted by ID ascending
- [ ] `erg list --help` documents the command
- [ ] Integration test covering open-only, --all, and --json modes
